<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Local Areas</span>
<h1>Soc Son by Motorbike: Motorbike Rental Planning in Hanoi</h1>
<p>Soc Son is Hanoi&rsquo;s northern gateway, the wide, half-rural district out past the city&rsquo;s northern edge where the airport keeps its fields, the villages keep their pace and the streets give way to roads, and for a rental rider it is the honest opposite of a lakeside base, long deliberate legs instead of doorstep ones, open riding instead of dense grids, and a plan that lives or dies by its planning. A stay here suits the rider with reasons, work, family, a long layover turned into a week, or a taste for the northern riding the district opens, and this page plans it honestly, from the verified counter at Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, across the city on the river&rsquo;s other side.</p>
<p>Start at the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/">Old Quarter motorbike rental</a> hub, see the machines and the verified prices at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> guide, browse the wider <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a>, read the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/long-bien-rental-planning/">Long Bien rental planning</a> page for the shop&rsquo;s own district, and see the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/bac-tu-liem-rental-planning/">Bac Tu Liem rental planning</a> page for the modern district on the northern run&rsquo;s way.</p>
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#sec-1">The district&rsquo;s position</a></li>
